ID: vr-47
Title: Separate editable head controls from read-only and creation-time settings

Status: DONE
Milestone: The manager clearly separates what can be changed now from fixed/unavailable values.
Dependencies: vr-45, vr-46

Purpose:
Owner requests two head-control sections: editable controls and settings that
cannot be edited after creation. Do not falsely classify disabled live controls
as permanently fixed; mode and speech activity can temporarily disable them.

Tasks:
[x] Split the manager into Editable now and Read-only settings.
[x] Show immutable session name/model with explicit creation-time explanation.
[x] Group disabled live controls separately with honest temporary-availability copy.
[x] Qualify regrouping, readiness, selection/focus isolation and settings forwarding.
[x] Update chapter/index/ledger, issue/Project and owned continuity.

Acceptance criteria:
Every runtime control appears once in its correct current-availability section.
Session name/head variant are read-only and explicitly set at creation.
Disabled live controls are not claimed to require recreation; regroup after
mode/activity changes. No controls are silently dropped or made writable.
Selecting another head cannot retain the previous head's focused controls.
Existing owner runtime/profiles remain untouched; no new model/speech behavior.

Completion evidence:
control-groups-02/controls-report.json records five actual-DOM fixture checks:
correct sections/creation labels, focused readiness regrouping, mode-dependent
disabled controls moving both directions, actual selected-head setting events,
same-schema head selection replacing focused identity/controls and narrow
section layout without internal horizontal overflow.
Actual manager HTML/JS/CSS in sandboxed Electron, deterministic API fixtures;
not a real-head/model or native speech qualification. Final selected-controls
screenshot inspected: both bordered sections and their explanations readable.
Initial01 screenshot retained;02 scrolls selected controls into view.
Development changes only manager HTML/JS/CSS; existing active pages are not reloaded.
Disposable native test profile; no real user head, microphone or camera needed.

Completion log:
2026-11-21 - Owner supplies head-controls screenshot and requests two sections.
Current disabled controls are mode/activity-dependent, not all creation-only.
2026-11-21 - Implemented two sections, immutable fields and precise unavailable
copy. Focus guard now checks same identity and availability: background updates
must disable/regroup stale controls; selecting another head cannot preserve old
focused controls. Request errors remain explicit; no backend/model changes.
